# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button with a ready BibTeX
# block. Most people cite when it is one click and skip it when they would have
# to construct the entry themselves.
#
# When the paper is on arXiv, add a `preferred-citation:` block below so the
# button points at the paper rather than at the repository. That is the
# citation you actually want accruing.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  JetSpace: measurement validity for frozen visual encoders in robot
  imitation learning
message: >-
  If you use this software, the cached representations, or the measurement
  protocol, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marshall
    given-names: Lee
    email: leemarshall1113@gmail.com
    alias: LeeMarshall1113
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/LeeMarshall1113/jetspace-imitation-learning
abstract: >-
  Frozen visual encoders for robot imitation learning are conventionally
  selected by how well a linear probe recovers actions from their features, and
  distribution shift is conventionally evaluated as a distance between latent
  sets. Neither convention has been validated against behaviour. This
  repository measures both: twenty-two frozen encoders are compared across
  multiple nuisance axes under a matched protocol, latent distance is
  calibrated against task success rather than against world-model internals,
  and session-to-session drift within a single laboratory is quantified as the
  reference floor under cross-domain comparisons. Predictions were
  pre-registered with named falsifiers before each experiment ran, the
  registrations live in docs/ alongside their invalidation conditions, and
  every deviation from them is disclosed. The failures are recorded alongside
  the results.
keywords:
  - robot learning
  - imitation learning
  - visual representation learning
  - frozen encoders
  - distribution shift
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
